    <h2 class="seal">State of Utah Financial Disclosures</h2>
    
<p>
	<u>Welcome to the State of Utah Financial Disclosures website</u>.</p>
<p>
	<u>Privacy Notice: The personal data provided on disclosures.utah.gov may be available to the public as provided by Section 63G-2-201.</u></p>
<div>
	&nbsp;</div>
<div>
	Click here to <a href="https://disclosures.utah.gov/Account/LogOn">log on and file a report</a>.</div>
<div>
	&nbsp;</div>
<p>
	<strong style="font-size: 18px;">Reporting Contributions and Expenditures:</strong></p>
<p>
	The general requirement for contribution reporting is to report each contribution you receive within 31 days of receiving it. However, there are additional requirements that must be followed:&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>
<ul>
	<li style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">
		<font color="#000000" face="Arial"><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Candidates must report each contribution within<strong> seven business days </strong>during the 30 days before the convention, primary election, and general election if they are contested by another candidate during that period. Failure to report contributions in a timely manner may result in a fine.</span></font></li>
	<li style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">
		<font color="#000000" face="Arial"><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">All expenditures must be reported by the reporting deadline for each reporting period.</span></font></li>
	<li style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">
		<font color="#000000" face="Arial"><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">All additional contributions received during a reporting period must be reported by the reporting deadline. </span></font></li>
	<li style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">
		<font color="#000000" face="Arial"><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">All filing reports must be filed by no later than 11:59 p.m. on the day of the reporting deadline. Failure to file a report on time may result in a fine and potential disqualification from the race.</span></font></li>
</ul>
